From c94e1233120ac5d7fb0c7233d19be94e301d94c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Le Bayon <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Jun 2021 10:56:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 142/954] feat(st-ddr): add STM32MP2 PHY driver

Based on A-2020.06 delivery (phyinit and firmware), and adapted to
our constraints in terms of system environment and coding rules.
Combines DDR3, DDR4 and LPDDR4 support with STMP32MP_*DDR*_TYPE flag
to reduce footprint impacts.

Fit features with platform scope:
- Simulation and Train 2D support removal,
- hard-coded number of pstates with capability check,
- use STM32MP_DDR_SKIP_TRAINING flag to enable specific code and
  remove skip_training=2 hybrid case,
- comment out all useless user custom functions,
- define PIE production codes as address/data static arrays,
- use generic firmware message block structure,
- uniform user input structures (int fields) and disable init/update
  (content is obtained from DT using base address get functions using
  a simple array method, so node/structure order must be identical),
- remove get/set Mb, get/set/override UserInput, setStruct and
  setDefault,
- remove all unused softSetMb() cases.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 278aa75d03e92a167281edf8f5152a083275a45f feat(st-ddr): add STM32MP2 PHY driver]
Signed-off-by: Nicolas Le Bayon <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
Change-Id: I4de3263e87f6f840340fdc55fc438b2ac8c4b206
